{{header}}
% Exercises extraction of straight line segments from top-level path objects.
%
% The page contains:
% 1. A 3x3 grid of separate stroked lines (4 horizontals and 4 verticals).
% 2. A horizontal line drawn as two touching segments.
% 3. A stroked rectangle (yielding 4 edges).
% 4. A transformed line under a 2x scale and translation matrix.
% 5. A closed subpath that starts with a curve (yielding 1 vertical edge and a
%    horizontal closing edge back to the subpath start).
% 6. A diagonal line and a short line.
% 7. Paths without straight stroked segments, which must be ignored:
%    - A cubic Bezier curve
%    - A filled-only rectangle
%    - A zero-length line
{{object 1 0}} <<
  /Type /Catalog
  /Pages 2 0 R
>>
endobj
{{object 2 0}} <<
  /Type /Pages
  /MediaBox [0 0 400 400]
  /Count 1
  /Kids [3 0 R]
>>
endobj
{{object 3 0}} <<
  /Type /Page
  /Parent 2 0 R
  /Contents 4 0 R
>>
endobj
{{object 4 0}} <<
  {{streamlen}}
>>
stream
% 1. 3x3 grid
50 300 m 350 300 l S
50 280 m 350 280 l S
50 260 m 350 260 l S
50 240 m 350 240 l S
50 240 m 50 300 l S
150 240 m 150 300 l S
250 240 m 250 300 l S
350 240 m 350 300 l S
% 2. Touching segments
50 200 m 200 200 l S
200 200 m 350 200 l S
% 3. Stroked rectangle
50 120 300 40 re S
% 4. Transformed line
q 2 0 0 2 10 10 cm 20 30 m 70 30 l S Q
% 5. Closed subpath starting with a curve
300 10 m 320 30 340 30 360 30 c 360 10 l h S
% 6. Diagonal and short lines
50 50 m 150 90 l S
300 50 m 305 50 l S
% 7. Ignored paths
200 50 m 220 80 240 80 260 50 c S
300 60 40 20 re f
10 20 m 10 20 l S
endstream
endobj
